UPDATE companies SET description='Old Capitol Food Company operates from Iowa City, Iowa, where it produces tofu using locally sourced ingredients. The company describes itself as a natural foods business focused on crafting tofu from 100 percent non-GMO organic soybeans grown in Iowa. No founding year or founder names are disclosed in public materials.

The company''s core activity is tofu manufacturing, centered on a supply chain that emphasizes Iowa-grown organic soybeans. Details about facility size, headcount, or production volumes are not published. The process highlights ingredient sourcing and craft production methods rather than industrial scale metrics.

Old Capitol Food Company supplies tofu to institutional and retail channels across Iowa. Named customers include the University of Iowa, Grinnell College, Cornell College, and the New Pioneer Food Co-op. Distribution extends to dining halls, grocery stores, food co-ops, Hy-Vee locations, and restaurants, indicating a focus on regional food-service and specialty retail markets.

The business states it was started to “spread the love of tofu” while holding itself to rising standards of environmental sustainability and responsibility. It emphasizes fostering deep connections with local vendors and neighbors as part of its operating philosophy.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tofu manufacturing", "Organic soybean processing", "Local ingredient sourcing"], "industries": ["Institutional food service", "Grocery retail", "Food cooperatives", "Restaurant supply", "Higher education dining"], "materials": ["Non-GMO organic soybeans (Iowa-grown)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% non-GMO organic Iowa-grown soybeans", "Direct relationships with local Iowa soybean growers", "Environmental sustainability as a stated operating principle", "Distribution through Iowa institutional and specialty retail channels"], "facts_used": ["Location: Iowa City, Iowa -> db", "Product: Tofu made from 100% non-GMO organic Iowa-grown soybeans -> /", "Customers: University of Iowa, New Pioneer Food Co-op, Grinnell College, Cornell College -> /", "Distribution channels: Dining halls, grocery stores, food co-ops, Hy-Vee, restaurants -> /", "Values: Environmental sustainability, local vendor connections -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Using 100% non-gmo organic Iowa-grown soybeans while fostering deep connections with our local vendors and neighbors, we seek to spread the love of tofu", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='old-capitol-food-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Oliveira Textiles was founded in 2007 in Bristol, Rhode Island, by textile designer Dawn Oliveira. After more than two decades in the textile industry, Oliveira launched the company with a focus on healthful surroundings, introducing "The Ocean Collection" of contemporary coastal patterns printed on hemp and organic cotton.

The studio produces stock fabrics and custom color options, selling fabric by the yard and finished pillows. Printing is done on hemp and organic cotton substrates. The operation runs out of a Bristol studio Byfield Building, and also offers freelance design collaborations and licensing opportunities.

Products are shipped worldwide via swatch requests, and the brand extends into design education through the "Design Me A House" podcast co-hosted by Oliveira and architect Katie Hutchison.

