UPDATE companies SET description='Olsun Electrics Corporation has operated from Richmond, Illinois since 1950, when it was established to serve the electronics industry in the greater Chicago area. The original manufacturing space occupied the back of a downtown Richmond building that housed a dentist office in front, where small thimble transformers were wound for a growing OEM customer base. In 1965, Gus Asta, one of the original partners, purchased the company and expanded the product scope to include power and distribution transformers and reactors.

The company designs and manufactures dry-type transformers from 5 kVA through 5,000 kVA in voltage classes up to 34.5 kV. All production occurs under one roof: design engineering, coil winding (barrel, disc, and block coils with wire and foil), vacuum-pressure impregnation varnish systems, miter and butt-lap core cutting, core-and-coil assembly, sheet-metal enclosure fabrication on CNC shear/punch/form equipment, structural base and clamp fabrication, powder-coat painting, encapsulation with polyester resin and silica sand, bus-bar fabrication in aluminum or copper, and final assembly with interrupter switches and tap changers. A Bystronic 4 kW fiber laser with automated material loading and unloading handles enclosure cutting.

On October 28, 2019, Olsun earned WBENC National Women''s Business Enterprise Certification, confirming at least 51% women ownership and control. The company emphasizes design flexibility for one-of-a-kind transformers alongside standard units, manufactures in the USA, and tests every unit to NEMA ST-20, ANSI C57.12.01, and C57.12.91, with designs meeting NEMA, ANSI, IEEE, IEC, ABS, and DNV requirements.', certifications=ARRAY['WBENC Women''s Business Enterprise Certification','UL Listed','cUL Listed','NEMA ST-20','ANSI C57.12.01','ANSI C57.12.91','NEMA standards','ANSI standards','IEEE requirements','IEC requirements','ABS requirements','DNV requirements']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design engineering for custom transformers", "Coil winding (barrel, disc, block coils with wire and foil)", "Vacuum pressure impregnation (VPI) varnish system", "Miter and butt lap core cutting", "Core and coil assembly", "Sheet metal enclosure fabrication (CNC shear, punch, form)", "Structural base and clamp fabrication", "Powder coat painting (multi-stage wash, electrostatic, oven cure)", "Encapsulation (polyester resin and silica sand)", "Bus bar fabrication (aluminum and copper)", "Final assembly with switches and tap changers", "Retrofit and replacement transformer design", "EV charging station transformer solutions (LV and MV substations)", "Fiber laser cutting (Bystronic 4kW with material automation)", "UL/cUL listed dry type transformer manufacturing", "Testing to NEMA ST-20, ANSI C57.12.01, C57.12.91"], "industries": ["Universities and colleges", "Petrochemical plants", "Oil and gas drilling", "Renewable natural gas / biogas", "Battery energy storage systems", "Municipal power utilities", "Marine / ship-to-shore cranes", "Architectural glass fabrication", "Commercial HVAC manufacturers", "Natural gas power generation", "Hospitals and medical facilities", "Hospitality and resorts", "Rail and transit", "Refineries", "OEM brand-label electrical manufacturers"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Copper", "Steel channel, angle, bar stock", "Polyester resin", "Silica sand", "Epoxy varnish", "Magnet wire", "Foil conductor", "Electrical steel (core laminations)"], "equipment": ["Bystronic 4kW Fiber Laser Cutting Machine with Material Loading and Unloading Automation", "Miter and butt lap core cutters", "Stacking table fixtures", "Vacuum pressure chamber for VPI", "Dip tank for varnish", "Computer controlled shear, punch, and form equipment", "Multi-stage wash and pretreat system", "Electrostatic powder coat spray system", "Oven for powder coat curing", "Cranes (2 to 20 ton capacity) - six units"], "volume": "5 kVA through 5,000 kVA, voltage classes through 34.5 kV", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["WBENC-certified Women''s Business Enterprise (51% women-owned and controlled)", "Family-owned and operated since 1965 with in-house craftsmen building each transformer", "Full vertical integration: design, winding, core cutting, enclosure laser cutting, powder coating, and assembly under one roof", "Bystronic 4 kW fiber laser with automated material handling for sheet metal enclosures", "86,000 sq ft facility with six cranes (2\u201320 ton) for large-unit handling"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1950 in Richmond, Illinois -> /about-us", "Gus Asta purchased company in 1965 -> /about-us", "Family-run, employs craftsmen and women -> /about-us", "86,000 sq ft facility, 35 ft walls, six cranes (2-20 ton), interior depressed truck dock -> /about-us", "Dry type transformers 5 kVA through 5,000 kVA, voltage classes through 34.5 kV -> /about-us", "WBENC Women''s Business Enterprise Certification October 28, 2019 -> /about-us", "Manufactured in USA -> /about-us", "OEM brand labeling since 1960s -> /about-us", "Design engineering, coil winding, VPI varnish, miter/butt lap cores, core/coil assembly, enclosure fabrication, base/clamp fabrication, powder coat, encapsulation, bus bar, final assembly -> /capabilities", "Bystronic 4kW fiber laser with automation for sheet metal enclosures -> /capabilities and /", "Retrofit capability -> /capabilities", "EV charging solutions (LV and MV substations) -> /capabilities", "One-of-a-kind custom transformer design -> /capabilities", "Industries: universities, petrochemical, oil & gas, renewable natural gas, battery storage, municipal power, marine, architectural glass, HVAC, natural gas power, hospitals, hospitality, rail, refinery, OEM -> / and /about-us", "Testing to NEMA ST-20, ANSI C57.12.01, C57.12.91 -> /about-us", "Designs to NEMA, ANSI, IEEE, IEC, ABS, DNV -> /about-us", "UL/cUL marks -> /about-us", "Materials: aluminum, copper, steel, polyester resin, silica sand, epoxy varnish, wire, foil, electrical steel -> /capabilities and /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Olsun Electrics is a leading dry type transformer manufacturing company that has been providing solutions in the most challenging environments and applications for over seven decades.", "founded_year": "1950", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/olsun-electrics/"], "ownership_tags": ["Women-owned", "Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='olsun-electrics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Olympic Controls Corporation was founded in 1968 and operates from a 61,000-square-foot facility in Bartlett, Illinois, and a 25,000-square-foot facility in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.

The company manufactures a range of electrical components including switchgear and transformer components (under the Electromagnetic Industries® brand), custom transformers (Acutran®), T-Bar® switches, fuel pumps, relays, and custom-wound coils.

Its customer base includes major defense contractors such as BAE Systems, General Dynamics, Lockheed Martin, and Raytheon Technologies, as well as industrial firms like Eaton and Siemens, and U.S. military branches including the Air Force, Navy, and Department of Defense. The company also supplies the aerospace, avionics, data center, solar farm, and power distribution sectors.

