UPDATE companies SET description='Olympus Manufacturing operates from Orem, Utah. The company was founded by brothers Jake and Matt Crowder, who started the business out of a passion for creation and a desire to help other brands bring their ideas to life. Their journey began with a love for making things and a recognition of the challenges entrepreneurs face when launching new products.

The company provides custom manufacturing and private label services focused on dietary supplements. Custom manufacturing covers formula development, ingredient selection, and packaging design tailored to a brand’s specifications. Private label offerings include a selection of stock formulations that clients can brand with their own packaging. Olympus emphasizes low minimum order quantities to accommodate both startups and established companies.

Clients range from aspiring entrepreneurs launching their first supplement line to established businesses expanding their product portfolios.

Olympus differentiates itself through personalized support and flexible production runs. The founders state that they pride themselves on offering low minimum order quantities and hands‑on guidance, ensuring each brand has the resources to succeed.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom supplement formulation", "Private label manufacturing", "Formula development", "Ingredient selection", "Packaging design and labeling", "Low minimum order quantity production"], "industries": ["Dietary supplements", "Nutraceuticals", "Health and wellness"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low minimum order quantities", "Personalized support throughout development", "Custom formula development and ingredient selection", "Ready-made stock formulations for private label", "Flexible solutions for both startups and established brands"], "facts_used": ["Founded by brothers Jake and Matt Crowder -> db", "Headquartered in Orem, Utah -> db", "Offers custom manufacturing and private label services for supplements -> page /", "Provides low minimum order quantities and personalized support -> page /", "Serves aspiring entrepreneurs and established businesses -> page /", "Focus on supplement formulation, ingredient selection, packaging design -> page /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom manufacturing and private label services", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='olympus-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Omni Defense Tech is based in Colchester, Vermont, and was founded on November 20, 1998, by electromechanical engineer Mark Harvie. The company began as a small engineering firm driven by Harvie''s passion for aviation and technology.

Today the company designs, develops, and manufactures the SKYDRATE in-flight bladder relief system, including male and female configurations and a certified through-suit connector that maintains environmental seals for immersion suits and CBRN personal protection gear. With eleven U.S. patents, Omni Defense Tech also collaborates with NASA to adapt its waste-management technology for astronaut missions, and its products are deployed worldwide.

The systems serve military aviators across the U.S. Air Force, U.S. Navy, and partner nations, as well as chem-bio personnel, search-and-rescue teams, and medical professionals. A female F-15E pilot noted the system eliminates the need to unstrap from safety restraints, simplifying cockpit operations.

Harvie founded the company to elevate human performance through safe, non-invasive, hands-off, automatic, and leak-proof relief solutions. The SKYDRATE system passes rigorous USAF and USN flight-safety standards and is marketed as "Certified Safe-To-Fly," reflecting a focus on mission readiness without compromising pilot restraint.', certifications=ARRAY['Certified Safe-To-Fly','U.S. Air Force flight safety standards','U.S. Navy flight safety standards']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and development of in-flight bladder relief systems", "Manufacturing of SKYDRATE male and female relief products", "Through-suit connector integration and environmental sealing", "Flight safety testing to USAF and USN standards", "Patent development and IP management", "NASA collaboration for space waste management"], "industries": ["Military aviation", "Chemical-biological protection", "Search and rescue", "Medical equipment", "Aerospace / space exploration"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified Through-Suit Connector maintains environmental seal for immersion suits and CBRN gear", "Does not require unstrapping from safety restraint systems for use", "Safe, non-invasive, hands-off, automatic, leak-proof design", "Eleven U.S. patents", "NASA partnership for space waste-management systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded November 20, 1998 by Mark Harvie -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Colchester, Vermont -> db", "Designs, develops, manufactures SKYDRATE in-flight bladder relief systems -> / and /about-us", "Eleven U.S. patents -> /about-us", "Partnership with NASA for space waste management -> /about-us", "Products used by USAF, USN, partner nations -> /", "Certified Safe-To-Fly, passes rigorous USAF/USN standards -> /", "Through-Suit Connector maintains environmental seal for immersion suits and CBRN gear -> /", "Serves military, chem-bio, search and rescue, medical equipment -> / and /about-us", "Testimonia