UPDATE companies SET description='One Semiconductor is headquartered in Austin, Texas, and was founded in 2011. The company began as a specialist in semiconductor equipment lifecycle solutions, focusing on refurbishment, upgrades, and maintenance for etch and deposition systems used in 200 mm and 300 mm wafer fabrication.

The company provides a range of services including equipment refurbishment and overhaul, technology upgrades and controller retrofits, sub-assembly repair and parts supply, and on-site field service with preventive and corrective maintenance. It also offers precision component manufacturing and thermal management solutions, with a product line of solid-state chillers in development. Operations span a global network across North America, Asia, and Latin America.

One Semiconductor serves wafer fabrication facilities, test and inspection platforms, and assembly operations within the semiconductor manufacturing industry. Its customers include OEMs and fabs seeking to extend equipment life, reduce downtime, and avoid capital expenditure on new tools.

The company emphasizes engineering-driven solutions with transparent execution, citing proven experience, global reach, fast response times, and cost-effective alternatives to equipment replacement as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Equipment refurbishment", "Equipment upgrades and retrofits", "Controller retrofits", "System conversions", "Thermal management solutions", "Sub-assembly repair", "Parts supply and sourcing", "On-site field service", "Preventive maintenance", "Corrective maintenance", "Equipment overhaul", "Precision component manufacturing", "Lifecycle management for 200mm and 300mm tools", "Etch and deposition system expertise"], "industries": ["Semiconductor manufacturing", "Wafer fabrication", "Test and inspection", "Assembly operations"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Etch systems", "Deposition systems", "200 mm wafer processing equipment", "300 mm wafer processing equipment", "Solid State Chillers (upcoming)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global service capabilities and fast response times", "Cost-effective alternatives to equipment replacement", "Engineering-driven solutions with transparent execution", "Proven experience in semiconductor equipment services", "Lifecycle solutions for 200 mm and 300 mm equipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2011 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Austin, Texas -> db", "Provides refurbishment, upgrades, conversion, maintenance for semiconductor equipment -> /", "Specializes in etch and deposition systems for 200mm and 300mm -> /", "Offers sub-assembly repair, parts supply, technology upgrades, on-site field service, equipment overhaul -> /", "Precision component manufacturing -> /about-us", "Global network in North America, Asia, Latin America -> /about-us", "Serves wafer fabrication, test and inspection, assembly operations -> /about-us", "Differentiators: global reach, fast response, cost-effective alternatives, engineering-driven solutions -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "One Semiconductor is a leading provider of refurbishment, upgrade, conversion, and maintenance solutions for semiconductor manufacturing equipment.", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='one-semiconductor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ontogen Medtech is based in Lisle, Illinois, and began operations in 2021 with a mission to give medical device innovators a strategy-focused, capital-efficient path from concept to commercialization.

The firm operates as a single partner for end-to-end medical device development and contract manufacturing. Its services span design, prototyping, engineering, testing and validation, regulatory support, and ISO 13485-certified production.

Ontogen''s work covers electro-mechanical, reusable, surgical, single-use, and diagnostic devices, and the company highlights its role in helping clients secure grants, patents, and FDA clearances.

Ontogen says its differentiation lies in keeping regulatory strategy, engineering, verification, quality systems, and manufacturing aligned under one roof to eliminate handoff gaps. It emphasizes hands-on execution by senior talent rather than advisory-only engagements, and it focuses on deliverables that de-risk programs—clear requirements, disciplined design controls, and verification plans that withstand scrutiny.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design", "Prototyping", "Engineering", "Testing & Validation", "Contract Manufacturing", "Regulatory Support", "Quality Systems", "ISO 13485 Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Medical device development"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One partner, end-to-end from regulatory strategy through ISO 13485 manufacturing", "Hands-on team integration with senior talent executing prototyping, engineering, and testing", "Evidence over activity: deliverables that de-risk programs (requirements, design controls, verification plans)", "Transparency in process and spend"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Lisle, Illinois -> db", "Founded in 2021 with mission to provide strategy-focused, capital-efficient pathway -> /about", "Services: design, prototyping, engineering, testing & validation, contract manufacturing, regulatory support, ISO 13485 production -> / and /about", "Thousands of devices shipped nationwide -> /", "Clients: Flow Medical, Stiehl Tech, Innoblative, Hubly Surgical -> /", "Device types: electro-mechanical, reusable, surgical, single-use, diagnostic -> /", "Differentiators: one partner end-to-end, hands-on team integration, evidence not activity, transparency -> /about", "ISO 13485 certification -> db and /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Manufacturing\nISO 13485 Certified Production", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/ontogenmedtech/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ontogen-medtech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Onyx Electronics Inc. has operated from Olathe, Kansas, since its founding in 1990. The company was established to manufacture precision pressure instrumentation for industrial markets, though the names of its founders and its ownership structure have not been publicly disclosed.

The firm produces pressure sensors, transmitters, and related instrumentation, and it also integrates those devices with process control panels, telemetry systems, SCADA software, and data logging equipment. Its capabilities span both the fabrication of sensing hardware and the assembly of complete monitoring and control packages, though facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not published.

Onyx serves industrial customers that require pressure measurement and control, including applications in process automation, remote telemetry, and supervisory control and data acquisition (SCADA) systems. The company does not list specific end-user sectors or named clients in its public materials.

