UPDATE companies SET description='Paragon Woodworking operates from a single shop floor in Pleasant View, Utah, serving nine counties across the Wasatch Front. The studio was founded in 2015 by Jon Anglesey, who brought 35 years of hands-on cabinetmaking experience to the venture. Anglesey remains directly involved in every design and layout that passes through the studio.

The company produces architectural-grade custom cabinetry and millwork for luxury residential interiors, specializing in frameless kitchen construction, bespoke vanities, integrated library systems, entertainment hubs, laundry rooms, and tailored closets. Two product lines share a common platform: the Custom Shop Series offers unrestricted design with shadow-line detailing and integrated LED lighting, while the ECO Line standardizes flat-slab profiles with pre-engineered subcrowns to cut installation time by two-thirds and reduce cost by 25–35%. Construction relies on interlocking blind-dado joinery, glued and screwed at every joint, with 3/4-inch drawer sidewalls, 1/2-inch bottoms, and Salice rack-and-pinion full-extension slides rated 33–50 lbs above competing hardware. Finishes are Italian waterborne urethanes with a proprietary cross-linker, delivering zero-VOC, zero-HAPS surfaces.

Clients include architects, designers, builders, and homeowners across Salt Lake, Davis, Weber, Summit, Cache, Box Elder, Morgan, Utah, and Wasatch counties. Projects range from new custom homes to full remodels, with the studio managing design, engineering, fabrication, and white-glove installation.

Paragon was started to elevate cabinetry from a trade to an architectural discipline, emphasizing total transparency in materials and pricing, continuous technical refinement, environmental stewardship through low-emission materials, and architectural respect for the client''s space and investment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom frameless cabinetry", "Architectural millwork", "Bespoke kitchen cabinetry", "Custom vanity frameworks", "Integrated millwork & library systems", "Architectural entertainment hubs", "Laundry room cabinetry", "Tailored closets & built-ins", "Blind-dado joinery", "Salice hardware installation", "Zero-VOC finish application", "Design consultation & engineering submittals", "White-glove installation", "ECO Line streamlined fabrication", "Custom Shop Series bespoke fabrication"], "industries": ["Luxury residential", "Architecture & design firms", "Custom home builders", "Homeowners (remodel/new construction)"], "materials": ["CARB-compliant non-formaldehyde TFL", "Sustainably sourced lumber", "Architectural birch", "Dark textured walnut", "Luxe woven fabric", "Classic white melamine", "Italian waterborne urethane finishes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Interlocking blind-dado box construction glued and screwed at every joint", "Salice rack-and-pinion full-extension slides with 33\u201350 lbs higher load rating than major competitors", "Zero-VOC Italian waterborne urethane finishes with proprietary cross-linker", "ECO Line reduces installation time by two-thirds and cost by 25\u201335% versus Custom Shop Series", "Founder Jon Anglesey personally reviews every design and layout"], "facts_used": ["Location: Pleasant View, Utah -> /", "Founded 2015 by Jon Anglesey -> /about", "35 years bench experience -> /about", "Serves 9 Northern Utah counties -> /", "Two product lines: Custom Shop Series and ECO Line -> /, /services", "Blind-dado joinery, Salice hardware, ze