UPDATE companies SET description='Parts Unlimited Interiors operates from a 120,000-square-foot facility in La Grange, Kentucky, in the Oldham County Business Park. The company traces its origins to 1974, when Rollo Fox and his wife Colleen (née Morris) attended a Corvair collectors'' convention in Chicago and sold new-old-stock parts from their car trunk. Colleen''s father, H.V. Morris, had recommended the Corvair as economical transportation, and the couple''s early success selling surplus parts led them to advertise in enthusiast magazines and eventually reproduce Corvair interior components.

The company manufactures interior soft-trim and hard-goods for classic American vehicles, including seat upholstery, door panels, headliners, window felts, console carpet, and insulation products. Production spans GM (Chevrolet, Pontiac, Buick), Ford, and Mopar models. The La Grange plant houses over 100 employees, with more than 80 automotive interior artisans overseeing computer-controlled machinery. Approximately 97–98% of products are made in the United States, with the remainder sourced overseas.

Parts Unlimited Interiors sells primarily through a network of over 100 aftermarket dealers across the U.S. and internationally, offering wholesale and dealer pricing. Its customer base includes restoration shops, classic-car enthusiasts, and dealers specializing in muscle-car and vintage-vehicle interiors.

The business pivoted from reselling finite NOS parts to manufacturing reproductions when original supplies dwindled. After being acquired by Restoration Parts Unlimited in August 2013 and later by Classic Industries in October 2023, the company reports that raw-material lead times dropped from several months to two to three weeks, and dealer delivery lead times fell to under one month. The firm emphasizes its U.S.-based manufacturing, deep artisan expertise, and same-day or next-day shipping on stocked items as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Seat upholstery manufacturing", "Door panel manufacturing", "Headliner manufacturing", "Window felt manufacturing", "Console carpet manufacturing", "Floor insulation manufacturing", "Cab insulation manufacturing", "Door insulation manufacturing", "Kick panel manufacturing", "Package tray manufacturing", "Automotive interior soft-trim production", "Automotive interior hard-goods production", "Pattern reproduction for vintage vehicles", "Computer-controlled cutting and sewing"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Classic car restoration", "Muscle car restoration", "GM vehicle restoration", "Ford vehicle restoration", "Mopar vehicle restoration"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day or next-day shipping for stocked parts; less than one month for dealer deliveries", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["97\u201398% of products manufactured in the USA", "Same-day and next-day shipping available on stocked parts", "Wholesale and dealer pricing programs", "Over 80 automotive interior artisans, many with decades of tenure", "Dealer delivery lead times reduced to less than one month after Classic Industries acquisition"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 by Rollo and Colleen Fox -> /about-us", "Started selling NOS Corvair parts from trunk at Chicago convention -> /about-us", "Expanded from trunk to basement to Jefferson Trade Center (Dec 1984) to 51,400 sq ft Louisville facility to 120,000 sq ft La Grange facility -> /about-us", "97-98% products manufactured in USA -> /about-us", "Over 100 employees, 80+ artisans -> /about-us", "Acquired by Restoration Parts Unlimited Aug 2013 -> /about-us", "Acquired by Classic Industries Oct 2023 -> /about-us", "Lead times reduced to 2-3 weeks for materials, <1 month for deliveries -> /about-us", "Products: seat upholstery, door panels, headliners, window felts, insulation, etc. -> /", "Serves GM, Ford, Mopar models -> /", "Wholesale/dealer pricing -> /", "Same-day/next-day shipping -> /", "Headquarters La Grange, KY -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Parts Unlimited Interiors manufactures the finest interior soft trim products for the classic Impala models", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "over 100", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='parts-unlimited-interiors-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pascetti Steel Design, Inc. operates from Albuquerque, New Mexico. The company is a family-owned shop founded by Damian Pascetti, who spent his career in steel starting with his father''s structural steel business before opening Pascetti Steel Design. Management oversees every project directly, reflecting the small-shop structure.

The firm provides turnkey custom steel fabrication for commercial and residential projects. Its scope runs from design and shop drawings through fabrication, delivery, and installation. Core products include steel stair and railing packages, custom balconies, steel canopies, large-scale architectural light fixtures, perforated metal panels, shade structures, custom gates, signage, and public art. The shop also handles historic restoration metalwork and has developed a patent-pending gym equipment system called the Phat Rack™. Work is designed in CAD and prefabricated for field installation.

Projects have been delivered for commercial buildings, hotels and resorts, fitness facilities, municipal landmarks, and cultural institutions. Notable examples include the USS Albuquerque submarine monument restoration, the Penguin Chill exhibit at the ABQ BioPark, and historic railing restorations in Albuquerque, Durango (CO), and Dayton (OH). The company also supplies pre-finished aluminum balcony railing for hospitality projects.

