/", "Serves electrical contractors, engineering/design firms -> /", "Serves utilities PECO Energy, FirstEnergy (Met-Ed, JCP&L) -> db (industries_served)", "CAD/CAM system -> /about", "Adheres to UL, NEC, NEMA, utility standards -> /about", "ANSI certification -> db", "Mission to develop new solutions -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a designer and manufacturer of a complete line of electric power distribution products", "founded_year": "1938", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='penn-panel-box-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PennFab, Inc. is a Pennsylvania-based steel manufacturing company headquartered in Morrisville. The company specializes in structural steel fabrication for infrastructure and transportation projects.

Its capabilities span custom metal fabrication, bridge and large-scale fabrications, infrastructure manufacturing, and a full-service engineering department. The shop produces aluminum and steel gratings for walkways, catenary structures, signal bridges, handrails, equipment skids, mezzanines, and stairs, with welding services that include automatic welding machines. All material is melted and manufactured in the United States in compliance with the Buy America Act.

PennFab serves the railroad and transportation industries as a major supplier of track material, cable trays, wire ways, anti-fall equipment, and bridge bearings. Additional markets include material handling, highway and bridge construction, heat treating, furnace manufacturing, part washers, pollution control, flight and training simulators, water treatment, heat recovery, simulation chambers, and various OEM organizations.

The company emphasizes domestic production and adherence to industry standards such as AWS, AISC, ASTM, ASM, NYDOT, AREMA, MILL-STD, NAAMM, AASHTO, and OSHA. Testimonials from rail and construction clients highlight its quality, competitiveness, and long-term dedication to customer satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY['AWS','AISC','ASTM','ASM','NYDOT','AREMA','MILL-STD','NAAMM','AASHTO','OSHA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Metal Fabrication", "Bridge Fabrication", "Large Fabrication", "Structural Steel Fabrication", "Infrastructure Manufacturing", "Engineering & Design", "Welding (including Automatic Welding)", "Grating Fabrication (Aluminum & Steel)", "Catenary Structure Fabrication", "Signal Bridge Fabrication", "Handrail & Railing Fabrication", "Equipment Skid Fabrication", "Mezzanine Fabrication", "Stair Fabrication", "Material Handling Equipment Fabrication", "Pollution Control Equipment Fabrication", "Heat Treating Furnace Fabrication", "Part Washer Fabrication", "Flight Simulator Structure Fabrication", "Water Treatment Equipment Fabrication", "Heat Recovery Chamber Fabrication", "Simulation Chamber Fabrication", "OEM Fabrication Services"], "industries": ["Railroad", "Transportation", "Material Handling", "Highway & Bridge Construction", "Heat Treating", "Furnace Manufacturing", "Part Washing", "Pollution Control", "Flight & Training Simulation", "Water Treatment", "Heat Recovery", "Simulation Chambers", "OEM"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Structural Steel"], "equipment": ["Automatic welding machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Domestic production: all material melted and manufactured in the USA per Buy America Act", "Full-service engineering and fabrication under one roof", "Major supplier to railroad and transportation industries (catenary structures, signal bridges)", "Compliance with AWS, AISC, ASTM, AREMA, AASHTO, and other standards", "Automatic welding machines for complex fabrication"], "fa