The company positions itself as a direct source, advertising that it eliminates middlemen to offer fair pricing and prompt delivery, and it highlights a consultative approach to help customers choose the right wood for their specific applications. No specific certifications, tolerances, or lead-time guarantees are published. Customers can reach the business by phone, email, or through a contact form on the website.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hardwood lumber distribution", "Exotic wood sourcing", "Plywood supply", "Antique reconditioning", "Antique sales", "Product selection advisory"], "industries": ["Woodworking", "Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": ["White Oak", "Birch plywood", "Purple Heart", "Padauk"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Direct supply eliminating middlemen", "Fair pricing", "Consultative product selection", "Prompt delivery"], "facts_used": ["Location: West Fork, Arkansas -> db", "Product offerings: White Oak, Birch plywood, Purple Heart, Padauk -> home page", "Antique shop with reconditioned antiques -> services page", "Direct supply claim (cut out middleman) -> home page", "Fair prices claim -> home page", "Advisory service for product selection -> home page", "Prompt delivery claim -> home page", "Customer types: home or office, woodworking -> home page", "Contact methods: phone, email, contact form -> home page"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "High-Quality Hardwood Lumber & Exotic Wood Supplier in Arkansas", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='penny-hardwoods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pentar Incorporated, based in Huntsville, Alabama, was founded in 1998. The company operates as a contract manufacturer and full turnkey provider of electronic devices.

Pentar provides complete in-house assembly, test, packaging, and shipping services, alongside managed off-shore manufacturing. Its electronic assembly capabilities encompass surface mount technology (SMT) and through-hole processes, as well as full box build and mechanical assembly. The firm also offers design and development services including industrial design, analog and digital circuit design, embedded software development, and mechanical design using 3D modeling tools. A dedicated value engineering team evaluates products and processes to improve quality and reduce cost. Additional services include a service and repair depot with field returns processing and global drop-shipping logistics. Production scales from prototype quantities to high-volume runs.

The company serves telecommunications, consumer products, industrial, and medical markets. Notable engagements include a turnkey manufacturing partnership with Frederick Energy Products (FEP) for the HIT-NOT® pedestrian collision avoidance system, and production of GPS receivers used in cellular tower infrastructure. Pentar also manufactures products for the Recon Outdoors line of hunting and outdoor sportsman gear, as well as a variety of medical devices.

