UPDATE companies SET description='Phoenix Cable, Inc. (PCI) was founded in 1994 as a family-owned business in Phoenix, Arizona. The privately held company began as a local manufacturer of cable and wire harness assemblies and has since expanded its reach to serve customers globally.

PCI specializes in custom cable and wire harness assemblies, offering services that include automated wire preparation and crimping, custom cable labeling with Brady™ labels, reverse engineering of existing assemblies at no cost, and 100% inspection and testing to IPC/WHMA-A-620 standards. The company stocks a range of UL-style hook-up wire, jacketed cable from 1 to 60 pairs, coaxial cables (RG174 to RG217), flat ribbon cables, and Hi-Flex IGUS™/LAPP™ products, along with common connectors and contacts.

The company serves industries such as semiconductor, telecommunications, electronics, industrial, commercial, medical, and instrumentation. PCI has focused on semiconductor assemblies for the past 20 years, providing OEM-equivalent and custom assemblies for original equipment manufacturers and other clients worldwide.

PCI differentiates itself through reverse engineering at no charge, claimed shortest lead times in the industry, blind drop-shipping globally, and a quality system certified to ISO 9001:2015 with assemblers certified to IPC/WHMA-A-620. Membership in the Wiring Harness Manufacturers Association (WHMA) further underscores its commitment to industry standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC/WHMA-A-620','WHMA member']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire harness and cable assembly manufacturing", "Automated wire preparation and crimping", "Custom cable labeling (Brady\u2122 labels)", "Reverse engineering of existing assemblies", "Quality assurance and 100% testing", "Global shipping and blind drop-shipping", "Semiconductor cable assemblies"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Telecommunications", "Electronics", "Industrial", "Commercial", "Medical", "Instrumentation"], "materials": ["UL style hook-up wire", "Jacketed cable (1-60 pair)", "Connectors and contacts", "Coaxial cable (RG174 to RG217)", "Flat ribbon cable (9-64 position)", "Hook-up wire (24 AWG to 8 AWG)", "Hi-Flex IGUS\u2122/LAPP\u2122 cable", "Shielded PVC jacket cable"], "equipment": ["Automated wire prep and crimp tooling", "Specialized cable labeling equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Reverse engineering at no cost", "Shortest lead times in the industry", "Blind drop ship globally", "100% tested to IPC/WHMA-A-620", "ISO 9001:2015 certified"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1994 -> /about", "Family-owned, privately owned -> /about", "Headquarters in Phoenix, AZ -> /", "Manufacturer of cable and harness assemblies -> /", "Automated tooling for wire, cable prep and crimp -> /", "Stocks UL style hook-up wire, jacketed cable, connectors, contacts -> /", "100% final tested -> /", "Reverse engineering at no cost -> /", "Blind drop ship globally -> /", "Shortest lead times in the industry -> /", "Specializes in semiconductor assemblies for 20 years -> /", "Industries served: semiconductor, telecommunications, electronics, industrial, commercial, medical, instrumentation -> /capabilities, /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about", "IPC/WHMA-A-620 certified assemblers -> /about", "WHMA member -> /about", "Custom cable labeling with Brady\u2122 labels -> /services", "Global shipping -> /services", "Cable types: coaxial RG174-RG217, flat ribbon 9-64, hook-up wire 24-8 AWG, Hi-Flex IGUS/LAPP -> /capabilities", "OEM equivalent assemblies -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Phoenix Cable, Inc (PCI) is a privately owned manufacturer of cable and harness assemblies.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='phoenix-cable-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Phoenix Food LLC operates from Canton, Texas, where it has spent over two decades building a portfolio of dry‑mix products. The company was founded more than 20 years ago, though a precise founding year is not publicly disclosed, and no individual founders are named in its public materials. Ownership details such as family, veteran, or woman‑owned status have not been stated.

The business manufactures a wide range of dry mixes, including soups, entrees, biscuits, breads, baking essentials, desserts, no‑bake cheesecakes, and dip mixes. It runs two consumer‑facing brands—Homemade Gourmet and Just In Time Gourmet—and also produces private‑label products for partners. The company describes its operation as a diversified dry‑mix manufacturing facility with “excellent manufacturing processes and stringent quality controls,” and notes that it offers hundreds of existing formulations.

