UPDATE companies SET description='Planet Plastics Co operates from a 43,000-square-foot facility in Chino, California. The company has been in operation for over 50 years, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership details and founder names are not stated in available sources.

The company manufactures plastic lighting components—including diffusers and replacement lenses for fluorescent, LED, and HID fixtures—as well as point-of-purchase retail displays, motion picture and theme park props, food case displays, museum displays, spheres, hemispheres, and other custom fabricated products. Its processes encompass 3- and 5-axis CNC routing, CNC cutting, vacuum forming, drape forming, free-form blow molding, thermoforming, cylinder forming, laser cutting and etching, die cutting, printing, acrylic fabrication, drilling, sanding, sand blasting, gluing and bonding, flame polishing, buff polishing, line bending, and custom packaging fulfillment. The facility houses computerized panel saws, CNC routers, large-capacity ovens and presses, and thermoforming equipment. The company states it can ship quantities ranging from a single piece to millions.

Planet Plastics serves commercial, architectural, hospitality, OEM, and custom lighting markets, as well as specialty retailers, restaurants, and brand merchandisers for POP displays. It has produced components for entertainment projects such as Animal Planet’s “Tanked” visit, Iron Man arc reactor rings, and Jurassic World gyrospheres. The customer base also includes food service and museum sectors.

The company emphasizes service, customization, and a satisfaction pledge: every order is treated as the most important, rush orders are accommodated, and any quantity from one to millions can be shipped with custom packaging or kitting. Its large press forming capability and uniquely large oven capacity are cited as enabling projects that might otherwise seem impossible.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoforming", "Drape Forming", "Vacuum Forming", "Custom Shaping", "Cylinder Forming", "Blow Forming (Free Form Blow Molding)", "CNC Routing (3- and 5-axis)", "Precision CNC Cutting", "Laser Cutting & Etching", "Die Cutting", "Printing", "Acrylic Fabrication", "Drilling", "Sanding", "Sand Blasting", "Gluing and Bonding", "Flame Polishing", "Buff Polishing", "Line Bending", "Custom Packaging Fulfillment"], "industries": ["Commercial lighting", "Architectural lighting", "Hospitality lighting", "OEM lighting", "Custom lighting", "POP retail displays", "Specialty retailers", "Restaurants", "Brand merchandisers", "Motion picture props", "Theme park props", "Food case displays", "Museum displays"], "materials": ["Acrylic", "Polycarbonate", "PETG", "Expanded PVC", "ABS", "Styrene"], "equipment": ["Computerized panel saws", "CNC routers", "Large capacity ovens", "Presses", "Thermoforming equipment", "3- and 5-axis CNC routing machines", "Laser cutting/etching machines", "Die cutting equipment", "Printing equipment", "Sand blasting equipment", "Flame polishing equipment", "Buff polishing equipment", "Line bending equipment"], "volume": "1 to millions", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.005 in", "built_on": ["Ships any quantity from one to millions", "Custom packaging and kitting available", "Rush order capability", "43,000 sq ft facility with large press forming and oven capacity", "5-axis CNC routing and free-form blow molding"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Chino, California -> db", "43,000 SF facility -> /about-us", "Over 50 years in