UPDATE companies SET description='Plastech Inc. traces its roots to 1970, when Al Hendrickson founded an injection molding business in Rancho Cordova, California. The operation moved to Corvallis, Oregon, in 1976, initially running from a garage before expanding into a dedicated building at the Corvallis Airport Industrial Park. In 1996, Hendrickson''s son Michael purchased the company, incorporated it, and renamed it Plastech Inc. The business has remained family-owned for over 45 years and is still led by Michael Hendrickson, with his daughter and son-in-law serving as key employees.

Today Plastech operates from a 12,500-square-foot manufacturing facility complemented by 6,700 square feet of warehouse space in Corvallis. The shop runs seven injection molding machines ranging from 85 to 400 tons, supported by CNC machining, 3D printing, and rapid prototyping capabilities. The company provides a full range of services including tool and die making (both domestic and offshore), secondary operations, assembly, packaging, and design-for-manufacturing assistance. A family-oriented workforce includes 14 family members among its staff.

Plastech serves customers across a diverse set of industries, including electronics, dental, sporting goods, pool and spa, consumer products, trucking, industrial, education, medical, and aerospace. The company works with both domestic and international clients, offering turnkey manufacturing from initial part concept through to finished, packaged products.

The company''s stated mission is to be more than a manufacturer by building long-term partnerships through a customer-focused team environment. Plastech emphasizes competitive pricing and quality, leveraging over 20 years of strategic partnerships with three offshore tooling factories to manage tooling costs while keeping production domestic.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Tool and die making (domestic and offshore)", "Secondary operations", "CNC machining", "3D printing / rapid prototyping", "Assembly (electro-mechanical)", "Packaging / turnkey fulfillment", "Design for manufacturing (DFM) assistance", "Part design assistance", "Fabrication", "Post-molding CNC machining"], "industries": ["Electronics", "Dental", "Sporting Goods", "Pool & Spa", "Consumer Products", "Trucking", "Industrial", "Education", "Medical", "Aerospace"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["7 injection molding machines (85\u2013400 ton)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1970", "Seven injection molding machines (85\u2013400 ton capacity)", "Domestic and offshore tooling with 20+ years of offshore partnerships", "Turnkey services from design through packaging"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1970 by Al Hendrickson -> /about-us", "Moved to Corvallis, Oregon in 1976 -> /about-us", "Renamed Plastech Inc. in 1996 by Michael Hendrickson -> /about-us", "Family-owned for over 45 years -> /, /about-us", "Facility: 12,500 sqft manufacturing + 6,700 sqft warehouse -> /", "Seven molding machines 85-400 tons -> /", "Services: injection molding, tool & die, secondary operations, CNC machining, 3D printing, rapid prototyping, assembly, packaging -> /, /services", "Industries served: Electronics, Dental, Sporting Goods, Pool & Spa, Consumer Products, Trucking, Industrial, Education, Medical, Aerospace -> /about-us", "Employs 14 family members -> /about-us", "Offshore tooling partnerships with 3 fac