UPDATE companies SET description='PlastiCert operates from Lewiston, Minnesota, where it was established in 1981.

The company provides vertically integrated engineering, tooling, and production services. Its capabilities span standard and high-temperature thermoplastic injection molding (including PC, ABS, nylon, Ultem, Ryton, and PEEK), insert molding, overmolding, long-fiber and engineered resin processing, mold design and in-house tool construction, DFM and mold-flow analysis, mold transfer and recovery, and value-added assembly such as soldering and press operations. A Haas VM-3 CNC machine supports tooling work, and the press line includes a 55-ton machine among larger presses. PlastiCert targets recurring production volumes typically between 2,000 and 5,000 parts per month, adjusted for part size and complexity.

PlastiCert serves industrial, aerospace, medical, agriculture, electronics, and telecommunications sectors, with customers including a telecommunications antenna manufacturer, a medical device manufacturer, and commercial/consumer recreational product companies.

The firm differentiates itself by keeping engineering, tooling, and molding under one roof to avoid handoff gaps, emphasizing technical collaboration over commodity pricing. It has earned four Top Shop Awards from Plastics Technology magazine and positions itself as a partner for difficult programs requiring material expertise, insert complexity, or mold recovery.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (standard and high-temperature thermoplastics)", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Long-fiber and engineered resin molding", "Mold design and in-house tooling (design, build, repair, maintenance)", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) and mold-flow analysis", "Mold transfer and program recovery (evaluation, root-cause analysis, corrective work, sampling, validation)", "Value-added assembly (soldering, arbor press assembly)", "Prototyping (multiple prototype options)", "Short-run and recurring production", "Engineering support (material guidance, tooling strategy)", "CNC machining (Haas VM-3)", "Mold temperature control (water and hot-oil systems)", "Quality management (ISO 9001:2015)"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Aerospace", "Medical", "Agriculture", "Electronics", "Telecommunications", "Commercial/Consumer Recreational Products"], "materials": ["PC (polycarbonate)", "ABS", "Nylon", "Ultem (PEI)", "Ryton (PPS)", "PEEK", "Long-fiber resins", "Engineered resins", "Composite materials"], "equipment": ["Haas VM-3 CNC machine", "Injection molding presses (55-ton, large press line-up)", "Mold temperature control systems (water and hot-oil)"], "volume": "Prototype to 5,000 parts per month (recurring production typically 2,000\u20135,000 parts/month)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated engineering, tooling, and production under one roof", "In-house tool shop for design, build, repair, and maintenance", "Specialized in complex programs: insert molding, overmolding, engineered resins,