UPDATE companies SET description='Port Clinton Manufacturing Co. was founded in 1929 in Port Clinton, Ohio. The company has remained a closely held family corporation, locally owned and operated as a family business for nearly a century.

The shop specializes in high-value-added hardened, ground, and precision parts, with a focus on precision assemblies that mate components through brazing and mechanical fits. Its 68,000-square-foot facility houses 25 automatic screw machines capable of work up to 3-1/2 inches, supplemented by CNC lathes, CNC and multi-spindle chuckers handling blanks up to 12 inches in diameter, and a broaching department with 12 machines rated to a 54-inch stroke and 15 tons. Secondary machining covers grinding (ID, OD, centerless, double-disk, Blanchard), thread rolling, knurling, drilling, tapping, cross-drilling, deep-hole drilling, countersinking, honing, milling, tumbling, bead blasting, cut-to-length, grooving, slotting, trimming, and chamfering. Heat treating and coatings are managed through a qualified external network, while engineering, estimating, and tooling support are provided in-house.

The company serves diesel-engine applications for railroad, oil-and-gas mining, emergency power generation, and off-highway agricultural and construction equipment, as well as mechanical power transmission components such as mine safety devices, heavy-truck transmissions, and brake systems. It operates as a Tier 1 supplier to major engine manufacturers and counts several Fortune 500 companies among its long-term customers, some for over 50 years.

Port Clinton Manufacturing emphasizes total customer satisfaction and a zero-defect culture, backed by PPAP capability, a full inspection lab (CMM, optical comparator, surface finish, magnaflux, Rockwell hardness, ultrasonic cleaning, and Millipore particle counting), and a Dun & Bradstreet AAA rating. The owners’ personal attention to each account and continuous improvement in manufacturing efficiency are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automatic screw machining (up to 3-1/2\")", "CNC turning", "CNC & multi-spindle chucking (up to 12\" diameters)", "Precision grinding (ID, OD, centerless, double-disk, Blanchard)", "Broaching (internal/external, up to 54\" stroke, 15 ton)", "Thread rolling", "Knurling", "Drilling and tapping", "Cross drilling and deep hole drilling", "Countersinking", "Honing", "Milling", "Tumbling", "Bead blasting", "Cut-to-length", "Grooving", "Slotting", "Trimming", "Chamfering", "Precision assembly (brazing, mechanical fits)", "Heat treating and coating coordination", "Engineering, estimating, and tooling support", "Quality inspection (CMM, optical comparator, surface finish, magnaflux, Rockwell hardness, calibration, ultrasonic cleaning, Millipore particle counting)", "PPAP service"], "industries": ["Railroad", "Oil and gas mining", "Emergency power generation", "Off-highway agricultural and construction", "Mine safety devices", "Heavy truck transmission", "Brake system components"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["25 automatic screw machines (capacities through 3-1/2\")", "CNC lathes", "12 broaching machines (54\" stroke, 15 ton)", "ID/OD grinders", "Centerless grinders", "Double-disk grinders", "Blanchard grinders", "CNC & multi-spindle chuckers (up to 12\" diameters)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nearly a century of service, quality, and timely deliveries", "68,000 sq ft facility supporting Just-In-Time requirements", "In-house precision assembly 