n-manufacturing-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Port Plastics was founded in 1960 in Albuquerque, New Mexico, as a regional supplier of industrial plastic materials to local manufacturers. Over six decades, the company has grown into a national distributor with 11 strategically located facilities across the United States.

The company stocks more than 1,000 grades of high-performance engineering plastics — including PEEK, PTFE, polycarbonate, and acrylic — and operates in-house fabrication shops equipped with precision CNC machining centers, CNC routers, and panel saws capable of cutting material up to 5 inches thick and 11 feet long. Its fabrication services cover CNC machining to tolerances of ±0.001 inch, routing, drilling, thermoforming, and welding, supporting orders from prototype quantities to production runs. Same-day cutting and next-day delivery are available from its distributed inventory network.

Port Plastics serves semiconductor manufacturers requiring ultra-high-purity, FM4910-compliant materials for cleanroom environments; energy and oil-and-gas clients specifying NORSOK M-710-qualified components for subsea applications; aerospace and defense contractors relying on AS9100D-compliant quality systems and ITAR-registered facilities; medical and life-science companies needing USP Class VI biocompatible polymers; and food-and-beverage processors using FDA- and NSF-compliant materials for direct food contact.

The company positions itself as a technical partner rather than a pure material supplier, emphasizing its team of materials engineers who average 15-plus years of industry experience. It maintains deep inventory positions to buffer supply disruptions, provides full traceability documentation with every shipment, and holds ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, and ITAR registrations across its quality system.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D','ITAR registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom CNC machining (\u00b10.001 in tolerance)", "CNC routing", "Panel saw cutting (up to 5 in thick, 11 ft long)", "Drilling", "Thermoforming", "Welding", "Precision cutting services", "Material distribution and supply chain management", "Technical material selection and application engineering support", "Quality assurance and traceability documentation", "Same-day/next-day delivery programs", "Inventory stocking and vendor-managed inventory programs"], "industries": ["Semiconductor manufacturing", "Energy & oil & gas", "Aerospace & defense", "Medical & life sciences", "Food & beverage processing", "Renewable energy", "Commercial vehicle & heavy equipment", "Automotive", "Marine", "Industrial manufacturing"], "materials": ["PEEK", "PTFE", "Polycarbonate", "Acrylic", "PVDF", "PAI (Torlon)", "PPS", "Vespel\u00ae polyimide", "Ultem\u00ae PEI", "UHMW (FDA-grade)", "Acetal (FDA-grade)", "HDPE (FDA-grade)", "PPSU (Radel\u00ae)", "Polysulfone", "USP Class VI compliant polymers"], "equipment": ["Precision CNC machining centers", "CNC routers", "CNC panel saws (5 in thick, 11 ft long)"], "volume": "Prototype quantities to production runs", "lead_time": "Same-day cutting and next-day delivery for stocked materials", "tolerances": "\u00b10.001 in", "built_on": ["Same-day cutting and next-day delivery from 11 strategically located U.S. facilities", "Deep inventory positions maintained during global supply disruptions", "Materials engineers with 15+ years average plastics industry experience", "ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, and ITAR registered quality management system", "Full material traceability and compliance documentation with every shipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1960 in Albuquerque, New Mexico -> /about-us", "11 strategically located facilities nationwide -> /", "ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, ITAR registered certifications -> /", "Custom fabrication with CNC machining, routing, panel saw cutting -> /", "Tolerances of \u00b10.001 inch -> /", "Serves semiconductor, energy, aerospace, medical, food processing industries -> /", "Materials include PEEK, PTFE, polycarbonate, acrylic, etc. -> /", "Same-day cutting and next-day delivery -> /", "Materials engineers average 15+ years experience -> /", "Deep inventory positions during supply disruptions -> /", "NORSOK M-710 qualified materials for energy -> /", "FM4910 compliant materials for semiconductor -> /", "FDA 21 CFR 177, NSF, USDA, 3-A for food -> /", "USP Class VI, ISO 10993 for medical -> /", "AS9100D, FAR 25.853, ITAR for aerospace -> /", "1000+ material grades -> /about-us", "60+ years in business -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Port Plastics delivers industrial plastic materials and custom fabrication services to manufacturers nationwide through 11 strategically located facilities.", "founded_year": "1960", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='port-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Portland Bottling Company, founded in 1924, is headquartered in Clackamas, Oregon. The company has operated in the Pacific Northwest for nearly a century, establishing itself as a beverage co-packer. No founders are named in the source material, and ownership structure is not specified.

The company provides end-to-end co-packing services for ready-to-drink beverages in aluminum cans, including filling, secondary packaging, and warehousing. Its 500,000-square-foot footprint spans multiple facilities, with a state-of-the-art canning line capable of running up to 1,450 cans per minute. Processes cover cold fill, tunnel pasteurization, liquid nitrogen dosing, reverse-osmosis water treatment, and a range of can sizes from 8.4 oz to 16 oz. Automated cartoning handles 4‑ to 24‑pack configurations, variety packs, and registered film shrink wrap. On-site quality assurance labs and inline monitoring support FSSC 22000, HACCP, organic, gluten‑free, and kosher certifications.

Portland Bottling serves both national and independent beverage brands across the Western United States and Canada. Its customer base includes producers of carbonated juices, sparkling waters, energy drinks, functional beverages, coffee, tea, and carbonated sodas, with specialty certifications for organic, kosher, and gluten‑free products.

The company emphasizes proactive partnership, 24/7 production availability, and treating customer resources as its own. Its mission is to deliver the most trusted, safest, and highest‑quality RTD solutions while fostering a collaborative, family‑oriented workplace culture.', certifications=ARRAY['FSSC 22000','HACCP','Organic (Quality Assurance International)','Gluten-Free (Gluten Free Certification Organization)','Kosher (Orthodox Union)','Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Beverage co-packing", "Aluminum can filling", "Cold fill", "Tunnel pasteurization", "Liquid nitrogen dosing", "Reverse osmosis water treatment", "Cartoning (4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 24 pack)", "Variety packing", "Shrink wrap packaging", "On-site warehousing", "Off-site warehousing", "Quality assurance (on-site labs)", "Inline quality monitoring", "Organic certification (QAI)", "Gluten-free certification (GFCO)", "Kosher certification (OU)", "Batching", "Repacking", "Multi-packing", "Can sizing (8.4 oz, 12 oz sleek, 12 oz standard, 16 oz standard)", "Dilution ratios (1:3 to 1:5)", "Liquid and granulated sweetener handling", "Registered film shrink wrap"], "industries": ["Beverage manufacturing", "Food and beverage co-packing", "Ready-to-drink beverages"], "materials": ["Aluminum cans", "Liquid sweeteners", "Granulated sweeteners", "Reverse osmosis water", "Juice concentrates", "Flavorings", "Carbon dioxide"], "equipment": ["Canning line (up to 1,450 cans/min)", "Tunnel pasteurizer", "Liquid nitrogen dosing system", "Reverse osmosis water treatment system", "Automated cartoning and palletizing equipment", "Inline quality monitoring systems", "On-site QA laboratories"], "volume": "Up to 1,450 cans per minute", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Up to 1,450 cans per minute on a single canning line", "FSSC 22000, HACCP, organic (QAI), gluten\u2011free (GFCO), and kosher (OU) certifications", "500,000 sq ft of production, storage, and repacking space with 24