r nearly a century, Portland Bottling Company and its team across multiple facilities provides flexibility and responsiveness, with a wide geographical reach, as well as the scale to handle your needs.", "founded_year": "1924", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='portland-bottling-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Portland Garment Factory (PGF) was founded in 2008 in Portland, Oregon, by Britt Howard. The woman-owned studio began as a zero-waste creative design and fabrication shop aiming to upend the traditional factory model through ethical labor practices and environmental sustainability.

The company provides full-service soft-goods manufacturing, including custom cut-and-sew production (20,000+ units), art fabrication, product development, prototyping, and retail/experiential fabrication. Operations run in-house with a team of 11–50 employees, supported by an internal experimentation lab (PGF Lab) for material and process innovation.

PGF serves designers, brands, agencies, and artists across apparel, retail, experiential marketing, art institutions, corporate branding, food and beverage, sports, technology, and hospitality. Clients have included Nike, Adidas, Intel, Portland Art Museum, Tillamook, Xbox, Converse, UGG, and DiGiorno, among others.

The studio’s differentiation rests on its zero-waste commitment, B Corporation certification, WBENC woman-owned certification, and Sustainability at Work Gold certification. Core values—Be Human, Think Forward, Honor Process, Respect Time, Invite Challenge—guide a model that blends creative ideation with responsible production.', certifications=ARRAY['Certified B Corporation™','Certified Woman Owned Business (WBENC)','Sustainability at Work Gold Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cut-and-sew manufacturing", "Art fabrication", "Product development and prototyping", "Retail and experiential fabrication", "Ideation and concept development", "In-house experimentation (PGF Lab)", "Design (experiences, spaces, garments)", "Build (in-house production)", "Zero-waste manufacturing", "Sustainable fabrication", "Soft goods innovation", "Installation fabrication", "Mascot and costume fabrication", "Soft sculpture fabrication", "Textile printing and fabric painting", "Upcycled/recycled materials fabrication"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Fabrics", "Leather", "Recycled materials (NetPlus)", "Upcycled textiles"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to 20,000+ units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero-waste manufacturing studio", "In-house PGF Lab for experimentation and prototyping", "Certified B Corporation and WBENC woman-owned", "Ethical labor practices and Sustainability at Work Gold certified", "Full-service from ideation to high-volume cut-and-sew (20k+ units)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2008 in Portland, Oregon -> /about", "Woman-owned, Lady Owned -> /about", "Founder Britt Howard -> /about", "Zero-waste studio, ethical labor, environmental sustainability -> /about", "Full-service creative design and fabrication studio -> /about", "Custom cut-and-sew manufacturing 20k+ units -> /services", "Art fabrication, product development, prototyping, retail/experiential fabrication -> /services", "In-house PGF Lab for experimentation -> 