UPDATE companies SET description='Potter Webster Company has operated from Portland, Oregon since 1940 as a family-owned business. The company began as a local parts supplier and has grown into a nationally recognized distributor while remaining under family ownership.

The company stocks more than 120 product lines across a 51,000-square-foot warehouse, supplying components for commercial trucks and trailers. In addition to distribution, Potter Webster runs a service shop that performs light trailer repairs, machine-shop work, U-bolt bending, custom cable fabrication, fan-clutch rebuilding, and brake-shoe relining. The facility also supports hydraulic and PTO services, driveline work, and axle-system assembly.

The inventory features brands such as Hendrickson trailer-axle parts, Dana/Spicer drivetrain components, and Denso starters and alternators under the Power Edge label. Past acquisitions — including the assets of R.W. Conroy Company and Customer Parts & Trailer Supply — expanded the product range and led to the Custom Trailer Parts line.

