UPDATE companies SET description='Power Electronics International, Inc. (PE) operates from East Dundee, Illinois, where it designs, engineers, and manufactures its full line of motion control products for overhead cranes and hoists. The company focuses exclusively on crane and hoist applications, developing drives, soft-starts, and control systems tailored to those demands.

The product range includes Micro-Speed® variable frequency drives, Smooth-Move® reduced torque control units, Multi-Vector® closed-loop hoist drives, and a variety of control panels such as travel motion, hoist, multiple-motion, and custom configurations. PE also manufactures regeneration resistors for dynamic braking, the PE-SAM™ sensorless anti-swing system integrated into its Ultra Series drives, PE360™ rotation control for hook positioning, PLC-based automation for lifting systems, and the PE Mobi-Power™ wireless power system for mobile equipment. The company states that over a quarter of a million crane and hoist motions worldwide utilize its equipment.

PE serves overhead crane and hoist technicians, mechanics, and industrial material handling operations.

The company emphasizes an Upgrade-Path™ philosophy, ensuring that all past and present programming methods remain compatible with future drive models. All hardware is designed, engineered, and manufactured in its East Dundee facility, and its control panels and automation systems carry UL and cUL approval.', certifications=ARRAY['UL approved','cUL approved']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Variable frequency drive manufacturing", "Soft-start manufacturing", "Motor control product manufacturing", "Control panel manufacturing (travel motion, hoist, multiple-motion, custom)", "Automation systems (PLC automation)", "Regeneration resistor manufacturing", "Anti-swing control (PE-SAM)", "Rotation control (PE360)", "Wireless power systems (PE Mobi-Power)", "Custom engineering and design", "UL/cUL approved panel fabrication"], "industries": ["Overhead crane and hoist", "Industrial material handling", "Bridge cranes", "Trolley systems", "Monorails", "Gantry cranes", "Tower cranes", "Heavy-duty hoist speed control"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Micro-Speed\u00ae variable frequency drives", "Smooth-Move\u00ae reduced torque control units", "Multi-Vector\u00ae drives", "Ultra Series drives", "PE-SAM\u2122 anti-swing system", "PE360\u2122 rotation control", "PE Mobi-Power\u2122 wireless power system", "PE Regeneration Resistors", "PLC automation solutions"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Upgrade-Path\u2122 philosophy: all past and present programming methods are subsets of future drive models", "All products designed, engineered, and manufactured in East Dundee, Illinois, USA", "UL and cUL approved manufacturer of control panels and automation systems", "Patented sensorless anti-swing technology (PE-SAM\u2122) integrated into Ultra Series drives", "Wireless power solution (PE Mobi-Power\u2122) for industrial material handling"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: East Dundee, Illinois -> db", "Manufactures VFDs, soft-starts, motor control prod