UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Metalworks LLC operates from a shop on Dunbar Street in Fremont, Nebraska. The business was founded in 2019 as a part-time welding venture by a single craftsman working after hours, building a reputation one job at a time. What began with one machine and mobile repairs has grown into a full-time fabrication and welding operation serving eastern Nebraska.

The company provides three core services: mobile welding that brings equipment to farms and plants, repair welding for cracked or worn components, and custom fabrication from prints or rough sketches. In-house capabilities include a MultiCam 3000 waterjet with KMT pump, an Amada shear, an Amada press brake, Syncrowave AC/DC TIG welders, and MIG welding for production steel work. The shop works in stainless steel, aluminum, and mild steel ranging from 22-gauge sheet to structural plate, handling everything from sanitary food-grade vessels to heavy equipment buckets and trailer frames.

Customers span food processing plants that require sanitary stainless welds, agricultural operations needing field repairs on combines and tillage tools, trailer owners with hitch and gooseneck damage, and industrial shops requiring brackets, racks, guards, and one-off structural parts. The mobile unit travels daily across eastern Nebraska, covering communities from Omaha to Schuyler.

The founder''s intent was to keep work in-house rather than subcontract cutting and forming, shortening lead times and keeping a single point of accountability. The same tolerances demanded by food plants are applied to every trailer hitch and bracket, delivered at small-shop pricing with direct phone access.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mobile welding", "Repair welding", "Custom fabrication", "Sanitary welding", "Aluminum fabrication", "Structural welding", "Waterjet cutting", "Plate profiling", "Shearing", "Press brake forming", "TIG welding (stainless, aluminum)", "MIG welding (mild steel)"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Agriculture", "Transportation/Trailers", "Heavy equipment", "Structural/Construction"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Mild steel", "22-gauge sheet to structural plate"], "equipment": ["MultiCam 3000 Waterjet (KMT pump)", "Amada Shear", "Amada Press Brake", "Syncrowave AC/DC TIG", "MIG welding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house waterjet, shear, and press brake eliminate subcontracting", "Mobile welding service across eastern Nebraska", "Same-day quotes for most inquiries", "Sanitary stainless welding to food-plant standards", "Single point of accountability from quote to delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2019 -> db and page", "Headquarters in Fremont, Nebraska -> db and page", "Mobile welding service across eastern Nebraska -> page", "In-house MultiCam 3000 waterjet, Amada shear, Amada press brake -> page", "Sanitary/food-grade stainless welding for food processing plants -> page", "Works in stainless, aluminum, mild steel from 22-gauge to structural plate -> page", "Same-day quotes for most inquiries -> page", "Started as part-time one-person operation -> page"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We weld stainless, aluminum, and steel \u2014 at our shop on Dunbar Street, or on site with the truck.", "founded_year": "2019", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='precision-metalworks-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Technologies, Inc., operating as Precision PCB, is headquartered in Elgin, Illinois.

The company offers a full suite of PCB services including design, fabrication, and assembly. Its fabrication capabilities cover single-sided, double-sided, and multilayer boards up to rigid-flex and HDI constructions, as well as RF/microwave and semiconductor PCBs. Assembly services include surface-mount placement down to 0201 passives, through-hole, mixed-technology, and leadless packages such as BGA, QFN, and LGA, all inspected to IPC-A-610 Class III. Production spans prototype through medium-volume runs, leveraging both domestic and offshore facilities.

Precision PCB serves customers in defense and aerospace, medical devices, automotive, LED lighting, industrial equipment, test and measurement, transportation, and networking and AI infrastructure. Its client base ranges from engineering teams needing quick-turn prototypes to buyers managing scheduled production deliveries.

